## Context
All four reviewers flag circularity: the author's group seeded reference-derived
content into Wikipedia (2019), then Wikipedia coverage is used as the
parametric-recall "ceiling" in §5/Figure 3. Reviewers: treat it as an
availability indicator / upper bound, not a neutral recall expectation; prefer
built-fleet-only coverage (where the contamination argument is strongest);
acknowledge the forward-looking tail postdates the 2019 injection. Tracker: 0644.
Reviews: openai_grinchy (obj 2), mistral_grinchy (obj 2), openai_student
(concern 2), mistral_student (§5).

## Action
- Reword §5 prose + Figure 3 caption + abstract: Wikipedia coverage is an
  availability/upper bound, not "models should recover this".
- Prefer the built-fleet coverage framing; note the forward-looking tail is not
  in Wikipedia. Wording/framing only — no data change.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] §5 / Figure 3 / abstract no longer assert Wikipedia coverage as an expected recall ceiling
- [ ] manuscript builds; adherence tests pass
